# ---- Agent instructions (not for distribution) -------------------------
.github/instructions/

# SpecStory transcripts live in the private confidential repo (symlinked).
# Slash-less form is the ONLY one that matches a symlink; slash form covers
# a real directory on machines not yet migrated.
.specstory
.specstory/

# Agent scratch. Two hazards from one entry: without it a `git add -A` commits
# scratch output, AND a bare `pytest` collects tmp/, so a stray test_*.py there
# silently joins the suite and corrupts the counts (see norecursedirs in
# pyproject.toml, which closes the second).
#
# Both forms, for the same reason as .specstory above: a trailing slash
# restricts a pattern to directories, and git does not treat a symlink as one.
tmp
tmp/

# Linked worktrees (per agent-config convention: {project_dir}/worktrees/).
# Both forms, same reason.
worktrees
worktrees/

# OBO session state lives in the private confidential repo, reached through a
# relative symlink. A session records whatever task is in flight -- item titles,
# descriptions, and the shell commands to run them -- so in a PUBLIC repo it is
# an open-ended disclosure channel.
#
# All four forms deliberately. A trailing slash restricts a pattern to
# DIRECTORIES and git does not treat a symlink as one, so the slash-only form
# stops matching the moment the path becomes a link -- which it now is.
.github/oboe_sessions
.github/oboe_sessions/
.github/obo_sessions
.github/obo_sessions/
